# Lien FX playbook (opt-in)

Use this when the operator **explicitly** asked for a Lien engine experiment.
Default analysis follows [docs/TRADER_KNOWLEDGE.md](docs/TRADER_KNOWLEDGE.md).
Research only. No orders. Full strategy tables: [docs/LIEN_FX_STRATEGIES.md](docs/LIEN_FX_STRATEGIES.md).

## Before a Lien technical setup

1. For one pair: `classify_regime` (oanda-research). For a universe: `scan_regimes`
   (max 32; default USD majors; aliases `lien-fx-ch4` / `lien-fx` for the
   book boards; other OANDA names as a CSV).
   Research pool: `agent/lien_pairs.py`. Default granularity **D** for this
   toolkit only — that is not the trader's "macro trend". Do not compute ADX,
   Bollinger, SMA, RSI, stochastics, or MACD in the model. Drop `trend_waning`.
2. Match the play class to the result: `join_trend`, `fade_range`, or `breakout_watch`. If `trend_waning` is true, do not aggress.
3. Optional: `mt4_draw_regime` on a **matching** symbol/timeframe chart (prefix `sbox.regime.`). Oscillators stay in JSON; the overlay is bands, MA stack, 10-bar high/low, channel rails, and a regime label. `classify_regime` includes compact `visual` rails (display only; not a Ch.15 entry). Paper/signal tickets: `mt4_draw_ticket` (prefix `sbox.ticket.`; hlines only, no orders).
4. Cite `lien-fx` via `rag-knowledge` (`search_knowledge` with `source="lien-fx"`,
   then `get_source_chunk`) **only for this Lien experiment**. Evidence is heuristic. Pin claims × chunk × engine
   with `python -m agent.fidelity` (add `--pin` when the corpus is ingested).
5. Journaled snapshot: `run_graph` with `engines` set (policy + `engine_candidates`). Measured test:
   `run_walk` (`ch7` / `mtf` / `lien`). MCP `entry_*` is a peek only.

## Risk template (library, not MCP)

Prefer ≥ 1:2 R, ≤ ~2% equity (`app/risk.py`). Scale half at 1R, stop to breakeven, trail the rest. Never add to losers.

## Entry engines

Ch. 8 (Multiple Time Frames) is coded as the `entry_mtf` tool (oanda-research): higher-TF direction gate + lower-TF RSI-dip/rally trigger, run after the regime filter. Ch. 9 is `entry_dbb`. Ch. 10/11/13/14/16 are `entry_lien(chapter)`. Chapters 12 and 15 are not tools yet (`breakout_watch` paper policy); use the doc tables only after the regime filter. Ch. 10 fades double-zero figures on M15 (20-SMA + 10–15 pip band); news/NFP is not encoded. Ch. 11 uses the calendar clock on OHLCV timestamps (`app/session_clock.py`). News/FOMC is not inferred from range fatness and is not an engine filter. Perspective hygiene: optional skip of **new** Ch.11 (and, for quiet-tape Ch.10, new) tickets on a scheduled FOMC **statement** London date (14:15 New York; frozen list `data/walk_gbp_usd_ch11_2015/fomc_calendar.json`). That is “never own the binary,” not a fitted edge — see [docs/LIEN_FX_STRATEGIES.md](docs/LIEN_FX_STRATEGIES.md) Ch.11. Do not flatten at 14:15 or restrict the engine to the next London date.

